# ask.patterns.example
#
# Patterns in this file trigger a CONFIRMATION PROMPT before the command runs.
# Claude Code shows the user a review dialog; they can approve or deny.
# Copy this file to ~/.clawband/ask.patterns and edit to customise.
#
# Format:
#   - One pattern per line
#   - Case-insensitive extended regex (grep -iE)
#   - Lines starting with # and blank lines are ignored
#   - These patterns are ADDED to the built-in ask list, not a replacement
#
# ── Examples ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Prompt before any production deploy
# deploy.*prod

# Prompt before database migrations
# prisma migrate deploy
# alembic upgrade head

# Prompt before stopping system services
# systemctl stop

# Prompt before any docker stop / rm
# docker stop
# docker rm
